{% comment %}
  Rebrand script statement — the teacher page's handwritten two-line heading
  over a narrow centred paragraph.

  The comp sets the first line in ink and the second in coral, so italic runs
  inside the heading take the accent colour the way every other rebrand
  section handles a two-tone line.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'saf-rebrand.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign sid = section.id
  assign pt_vw = section.settings.padding_top | times: 100.0 | divided_by: 1920.0
  assign pb_vw = section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 100.0 | divided_by: 1920.0

  comment
    On a teacher or artist page the paragraph under the script line is that
    person's bio, which the store already keeps as the collection description.
    Reading it here keeps forty person pages correct from one template and
    keeps them following the merchant's edits.
  endcomment
  assign body = section.settings.body
  if section.settings.use_collection_description and collection.description != blank
    assign body = collection.description

    comment
      A teacher page now opens with the first sentence of this same bio set in
      the script face, the way the artist comp draws it. Printing the bio whole
      again here would say that sentence twice within one screen, so the band
      picks up where the hero left off.

      The first sentence is removed by prefix rather than by rebuilding the
      string, and since 2026-09-18 it is found by the shared snippet rather
      than by a second copy of the hero's filter chain, so the two cannot drift
      apart. The snippet spaces out paragraph and line ends before strip_html:
      bios are written in a rich text box now (2026-09-14), and
      "one.</p><p>Two" would otherwise read "one.Two" and hide the sentence
      break.

      A few bios are a single sentence, so there is nothing left to hand over.
      Those used to print the whole description again, which put the same
      sentence on the page twice (Anina Deetlefs, Kristi Marié). Keagan's rule
      (2026-09-16) is that a person's bio never appears twice on a page, so the
      band now stands down entirely: no body, and no "More about X" heading
      over nothing. It comes back by itself once the bio gains a second sentence.
    endcomment
    assign skip_first = section.settings.skip_first_sentence
  endif
-%}
{%- if skip_first -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Where the first sentence ends is asked once, in
    snippets/rb-first-sentence.liquid, and the hero asks the same question of
    the same snippet. It used to be worked out here with its own copy of the
    filter chain, which is how Careshia Esperanza's page came to open "CARESHIA
    ESPERANZA STEENKAMP (b." up top and carry on "1991) is a South African
    self-taught artist" down here: two copies of one rule, disagreeing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture rest -%}
    {%- render 'rb-first-sentence', description: collection.description, part: 'rest' -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  if skip_first
    assign rest = rest | strip
    assign body = rest
    if rest == blank
      assign nothing_new = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- unless nothing_new -%}

<style>
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss {
    background: {{ section.settings.background }};
    padding-block:
      clamp(40px, {{ pt_vw }}vw, {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px)
      clamp(40px, {{ pb_vw }}vw, {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px);
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(16px, 2.19vw, 42px);
    text-align: center;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__heading {
    color: {{ section.settings.heading_color }};
    max-width: {{ section.settings.heading_width }}px;
    line-height: 1.45; /* the script needs air or the loops collide */
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__heading p { margin: 0; }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__heading em,
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__heading i {
    font-style: normal;
    color: {{ section.settings.accent_color }};
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__body {
    max-width: {{ section.settings.body_width }}px;
    font-size: var(--rb-fs-body-sm);
    color: {{ section.settings.body_color }};
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__body p { margin: 0; }
  /* Only between paragraphs, so a one-paragraph bio — which is all but two of
     them — keeps the exact spacing it had when this printed a bare text node.
     Set on the gap rather than on every p for that reason. */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__body p + p { margin-top: 1.15em; }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__body ul,
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ss__body ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25em; text-align: left; display: inline-block; }
</style>

<div class="rb-section rb-ss">
  <div class="rb-container rb-ss__inner">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <div class="rb-script rb-ss__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if body != blank -%}
      <div class="rb-body rb-ss__body">{{ body }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endunless -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Rebrand script statement",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "rb-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "heading",
      "default": "<p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, <em>consectetur adipiscing elit.</em></p>",
      "label": "Script heading",
      "info": "Italic runs take the accent colour — that is the design's second line." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body",
      "default": "<p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua.</p>",
      "label": "Body" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "use_collection_description", "default": false,
      "label": "Use the collection description instead",
      "info": "On a teacher or artist page that is their bio. To change the words, edit the person in the booking app (Artists or Teachers tab) or the collection in Shopify admin." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "skip_first_sentence", "default": false,
      "label": "Skip the first sentence",
      "info": "Switch on where the hero above already sets the first sentence in the script face, so the page does not say it twice. A one-sentence bio has nothing left to add, so the band hides until the bio is longer." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Colour" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background", "default": "#ffffff", "label": "Background" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "heading_color", "default": "#1e1e1e", "label": "Script" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "accent_color", "default": "#e07468", "label": "Script accent" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "body_color", "default": "#1e1e1e", "label": "Body" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Measure" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "heading_width", "min": 400, "max": 1400, "step": 10,
      "default": 900, "unit": "px", "label": "Script max width" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "body_width", "min": 300, "max": 900, "step": 10,
      "default": 640, "unit": "px", "label": "Body max width" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Spacing" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_top", "min": 40, "max": 400, "step": 5,
      "default": 190, "unit": "px", "label": "Top padding at 1920px wide" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_bottom", "min": 40, "max": 400, "step": 5,
      "default": 210, "unit": "px", "label": "Bottom padding at 1920px wide" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Rebrand script statement" }]
}
{% endschema %}
